## What I learned

- Taking logarithms turns exponential and power relationships into straight lines, so one tool (a line fit) handles all three model types.
- Plotting the same data on linear, semilog, and log-log axes is a fast way to identify the right model.
- Writing least squares by hand made it clear what `polyfit` is doing underneath.
- A high R² does not mean the model is right. Looking at the plot caught patterns (the wind power plateau, the thermistor curvature) that a single number hides.

